WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.176 --> 00:00:07.317
"Zann! Stop!"

2
00:00:07.537 --> 00:00:17.520
A sudden blast of energy grabbed Zann's body, flinging him back.

3
00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:21.381
He landed hard on the ground, several yards from the wormhole.

4
00:00:22.081 --> 00:00:24.442
When he looked up, the wormhole was spinning shut.

5
00:00:25.142 --> 00:00:27.803
A moment later Boz was hauling him up by the arm.

6
00:00:28.483 --> 00:00:30.143
The old man's face was livid.

7
00:00:30.163 --> 00:00:32.184
"What were you thinking?"

8
00:00:32.556 --> 00:00:35.459
Boz shouted, his long nose quivering with rage.

9
00:00:35.479 --> 00:00:38.461
"Have you gone mad, boy?"

10
00:00:38.481 --> 00:00:42.205
"How did you—" Zann didn't get a chance to finish the question.

11
00:00:42.965 --> 00:00:45.607
Boz snapped his fingers and zapped them both away.

12
00:00:46.348 --> 00:00:47.970
They landed in Teplo's living room.

13
00:00:47.990 --> 00:00:49.951
"You got him in time!"

14
00:00:50.332 --> 00:00:50.932
Gliss cried.

15
00:00:50.952 --> 00:00:52.654
"Thank goodness!"

16
00:00:53.855 --> 00:00:57.398
Zann ducked as Zing flew at him, blasting him with angry flames.

17
00:00:57.418 --> 00:00:59.740
"Quit it," Zann muttered.

18
00:01:00.684 --> 00:01:04.406
Glancing around, he saw Perda, Darb, and Teplo staring at him.

19
00:01:05.247 --> 00:01:06.107
"What's going on?"

20
00:01:06.127 --> 00:01:09.729
"Zing woke up and realized you were gone," Darb said.

21
00:01:09.749 --> 00:01:12.270
"He freaked out and rushed to find me."

22
00:01:13.071 --> 00:01:14.491
Zann scowled at the dragon.

23
00:01:14.852 --> 00:01:16.693
Then he realized what Darb had said.

24
00:01:16.713 --> 00:01:19.034
"Wait," said Zann.

25
00:01:19.354 --> 00:01:21.155
"What do you mean, he rushed to find you?

26
00:01:21.635 --> 00:01:22.816
You were in the same room."

27
00:01:23.896 --> 00:01:24.897
"Not exactly."

28
00:01:25.197 --> 00:01:26.298
Darb's face went red.

29
00:01:26.318 --> 00:01:30.300
"Um, I promised Gliss I'd meet her after midnight.

30
00:01:30.996 --> 00:01:34.157
I guess I didn't notice you were gone when I woke up and sneaked out."

31
00:01:34.917 --> 00:01:35.857
Zann looked at Gliss.

32
00:01:36.238 --> 00:01:37.138
She was blushing too.

33
00:01:37.158 --> 00:01:40.719
"I had something important to tell him," she said.

34
00:01:40.739 --> 00:01:43.080
"I'm leaving First City tomorrow."

35
00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:47.221
Zann just shrugged, thinking of what he'd overheard earlier.

36
00:01:48.081 --> 00:01:51.402
He wasn't surprised that Gliss was leaving for Swamp Bottom tomorrow too.

37
00:01:52.322 --> 00:01:55.443
Her parents and her uncle had been involved in the same meetings as Boz.

38
00:01:55.463 --> 00:01:58.484
"Whatever you say," he said with a smirk.

39
00:01:59.556 --> 00:02:03.898
"I think Darb would have figured out you'd left First City when he saw you in Swamp Bottom

40
00:02:03.918 --> 00:02:05.098
tomorrow with the rest of us."

41
00:02:05.118 --> 00:02:07.679
"Huh?" Darb looked confused.

42
00:02:08.040 --> 00:02:09.300
"No, you don't understand.

43
00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:11.861
Gliss isn't going back to Swamp Bottom.

44
00:02:12.561 --> 00:02:15.243
She's going on an expedition to the Cave of the Unknown."

45
00:02:15.263 --> 00:02:18.564
"What?" Zann whirled toward Gliss.

46
00:02:18.584 --> 00:02:21.305
"The Cave of the Unknown," he repeated.

47
00:02:21.325 --> 00:02:23.046
"Are you serious?

48
00:02:23.566 --> 00:02:24.786
Why are you going there?"

49
00:02:25.547 --> 00:02:28.448
The Cave of the Unknown was a remote and dangerous place.

50
00:02:29.316 --> 00:02:33.140
Few people had seen it, and even fewer had survived to describe it.

51
00:02:33.921 --> 00:02:35.663
Zann's parents were among those few.

52
00:02:36.363 --> 00:02:40.668
They had visited the Cave a couple of times, returning with many frightening stories about it.

53
00:02:41.849 --> 00:02:43.891
Staring at the floor, Gliss shrugged.

54
00:02:43.911 --> 00:02:46.514
"My parents are making me go."

55
00:02:47.375 --> 00:02:48.476
Zann hardly heard her.

56
00:02:49.157 --> 00:02:52.180
He was still thinking about all the stories he'd heard during his childhood.

57
00:02:53.008 --> 00:02:59.773
"My parents said the Cave of the Unknown is huge and really spooky, with countless tunnels and chambers,"

58
00:03:00.173 --> 00:03:00.514
he said.

59
00:03:00.534 --> 00:03:06.698
"The whole place is littered with ancient relics and manuscripts from the Old Times and stuff."

60
00:03:06.718 --> 00:03:12.923
"Yeah. Like the relics and texts Morb used to try to take over Magica," Perda said with a

61
00:03:12.983 --> 00:03:14.804
shudder. "Exactly.

62
00:03:15.144 --> 00:03:19.968
That's why the Red Council decided it's time to seal the place off," Teplo put in.

63
00:03:20.820 --> 00:03:24.801
"Until now they've relied on the Cave's reputation to keep people away.

64
00:03:26.081 --> 00:03:32.083
But after Morb's recent adventures, they don't want anyone else coming along and trying the same thing.

65
00:03:33.003 --> 00:03:37.405
The Council is sending an expedition to seal it off so the relics can't be removed."

66
00:03:38.085 --> 00:03:40.745
Boz didn't seem to be paying much attention to the conversation.

67
00:03:41.546 --> 00:03:45.087
His nose quivering wildly, he was still glaring at Zann.

68
00:03:45.867 --> 00:03:47.107
Zann recognized that look.

69
00:03:47.827 --> 00:03:49.768
It meant his grandfather was thinking hard.

70
00:03:50.752 --> 00:03:54.813
He was probably trying to come up with the perfect way to punish Zann for sneaking out tonight.

71
00:03:55.613 --> 00:03:56.794
Boz spoke out at last.

72
00:03:56.814 --> 00:03:58.894
"Enough about the expedition.

73
00:03:59.775 --> 00:04:03.056
We were discussing Zann's outrageous behavior."

74
00:04:03.896 --> 00:04:04.656
Zann cringed.

75
00:04:04.956 --> 00:04:06.077
Then he looked over at Darb.

76
00:04:06.097 --> 00:04:09.958
"So you saw I was missing and ran to tell Boz?"

77
00:04:10.298 --> 00:04:10.778
he asked.

78
00:04:10.798 --> 00:04:14.279
"I never thought you were the type to tell on your friends."

79
00:04:15.319 --> 00:04:17.640
"That's not what happened," Gliss said.

80
00:04:18.424 --> 00:04:22.046
"When Darb and I realized you were missing, we checked with Perda.

81
00:04:22.787 --> 00:04:27.710
She didn't know where you were, but she tried all your passwords and was eventually able to make

82
00:04:27.750 --> 00:04:28.631
your note appear."

83
00:04:28.651 --> 00:04:33.354
"I can't believe you didn't tell me you were going, Zann," Perda added.

84
00:04:34.074 --> 00:04:37.557
Her eyes flashed with anger, and her voice was cool and unfriendly.

85
00:04:38.658 --> 00:04:40.619
Zann hated having her look at him that way.

86
00:04:41.359 --> 00:04:45.242
He wished he could make her understand why he'd tried to go through the wormhole without telling his

87
00:04:45.282 --> 00:04:48.064
friends. But he wasn't sure how to communicate that.

88
00:04:48.904 --> 00:04:52.347
"Gliss came to us right away, thank goodness," Teplo said.

89
00:04:52.367 --> 00:04:58.132
"Since we knew you wouldn't be able to reach the palace wormhole, Boz guessed you might try the

90
00:04:58.212 --> 00:04:59.012
one in Wormwood."

91
00:05:00.033 --> 00:05:01.054
Zann glared at Gliss.

92
00:05:01.494 --> 00:05:02.915
"You ratted me out?

93
00:05:03.716 --> 00:05:04.877
I thought we were friends!"

94
00:05:04.897 --> 00:05:07.839
"We are," Gliss said, looking hurt.

95
00:05:07.859 --> 00:05:10.161
"I was trying to help you."

96
00:05:10.181 --> 00:05:12.003
"Help me?"

97
00:05:12.443 --> 00:05:14.385
Zann gritted his teeth, furious.

98
00:05:14.405 --> 00:05:18.428
"I helped you to reunite with your parents, remember?

99
00:05:19.176 --> 00:05:22.337
All you did tonight was stop me from doing the same thing!"

100
00:05:22.357 --> 00:05:24.458
"No," Darb said.

101
00:05:24.478 --> 00:05:26.798
"She stopped you from disappearing forever."

102
00:05:26.818 --> 00:05:28.939
"That's right, Zann."

103
00:05:29.339 --> 00:05:30.679
Boz sounded disapproving.

104
00:05:31.399 --> 00:05:32.340
He glanced at Teplo.

105
00:05:32.360 --> 00:05:37.401
"I'm starting to think it's a mistake to let Zann come along when we leave tomorrow."

106
00:05:37.421 --> 00:05:41.302
"You mean you might not take me back to Swamp Bottom?"

107
00:05:42.082 --> 00:05:43.123
Zann rolled his eyes.

108
00:05:43.483 --> 00:05:45.343
That didn't sound like much of a punishment to him.

109
00:05:45.363 --> 00:05:47.084
"Swamp Bottom?

110
00:05:47.528 --> 00:05:49.189
Who's going to Swamp Bottom?"

111
00:05:49.589 --> 00:05:50.149
Boz asked.

112
00:05:50.169 --> 00:05:52.650
"We are," Zann said.

113
00:05:52.670 --> 00:05:55.171
"I heard you two talking about it earlier.

114
00:05:55.912 --> 00:05:58.113
You said we leave tomorrow afternoon."

115
00:05:58.133 --> 00:06:00.994
"Yes, we do," Teplo said.

116
00:06:01.014 --> 00:06:02.695
"But not for Swamp Bottom.

117
00:06:03.435 --> 00:06:06.816
Your grandfather and I are part of the expedition Gliss mentioned.

118
00:06:07.617 --> 00:06:09.177
That means you're part of it too."

119
00:06:09.958 --> 00:06:10.698
Boz nodded.

120
00:06:10.718 --> 00:06:12.118
"That's right, Zann.

121
00:06:12.959 --> 00:06:15.420
You're going to the Cave of the Unknown."
